[?2004l[?2004h> "    (iii) $12,107, plus 31% of the excess over $53,500 if the taxable income is over $53,500 but not over $115,000;"
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Reasoning
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Charlie qualifies as a qualifying relative (dependent):**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Charlie is Alice's father → relationship test met under §152(d)(2)(C) (line 162)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Charlie has no income in 2015 → meets §152(d)(1)(B) (line 156)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Charlie is not a qualifying child → meets §152(d)(1)(D) (line 157)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Bob qualifies as a qualifying relative (dependent):**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Bob is Charlie's brother, making him Alice's uncle → relationship test met under §152(d)(2)(F) (line 168)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Bob has no income in 2015 → meets §152(d)(1)(B) (line 156)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Bob is not a qualifying child → meets §152(d)(1)(D) (line 157)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Alice's filing status:**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The case facts do not state that Alice is unmarried or that she maintains a household for her father Charlie
[?2004l[?2004h>    - The case facts do not state that Alice is married
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Therefore, Alice cannot establish head of household status under §2(b) (line 204)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Alice is treated as an unmarried individual under §1(c) (lines 29-40)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Exemption calculation:**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Exemption amount = $2,000 per §151(d)(1) (line 72)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Number of exemptions = 3 (Alice + Charlie + Bob)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Total exemptions = 3 × $2,000 = $6,000
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Taxable income = $87,319 - $6,000 = $81,319
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 5. **Tax calculation (unmarried individual under §1(c)):**
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Taxable income $81,319 is over $53,500 but not over $115,000
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Tax = $12,107 + 31% × ($81,319 - $53,500)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Tax = $12,107 + 0.31 × $27,819
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Tax = $12,107 + $8,623.89 = $20,730.89
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Integer tax = $20,730
[?2004l[?2004h> 
